ry calls in  toy shack owner johnny jimenez who puts  a comic's value at around ten thousand  dollars less than john's asking price  between six thousand and seven thousand  dollars according to jimenez the main  problem is the cover which includes a  prominent santa fe shipping stamp as  well as stains increases  jon tries to get corey to go as high as  ten thousand dollars but the most a big  house will offer is seven thousand  dollars  john's disappointment is understandable  two years earlier a high-grade copy of  amazing fantasy number 15  sold for 1.1 million dollars  unfortunately for him in comic book  collecting there's a huge difference  between mid-grade and high grade  i miss the part where that's my problem  in season 14  restaurant owner tommy brings in copies  of incredible hulk number one through  six  signed by stan lee himself in a story  that will amaze and terrify any comic  book collector tommy says he found them  while he was building his restaurant in  brooklyn  specifically quote in the basement  behind a whole bunch of garbage  i i see this as an absolute win  tommy's comics actually represent the  entire first series of incredible hulk  it only lasted six issues due to low  sales though the hulk would remain in  the marvel universe helping to found the  avengers eventually receiving his own  solo series once again and becoming one  of the most iconic superheroes of all  time  the only problem with the comics is that  stan lee's signature isn't original  tommy met stan the man and asked him to  sign the book several years earlier and  corey wonders if that may have devalued  the rare issues  especially because lee's signature isn't  all that rare so he brings in paul lytch  who puts everyone's mind at ease by  confirming that most buyers would be  thrilled about the signatures  eggshell  tommy wants forty thousand dollars for  the comics and paul roughly agrees  appraising them at thirty six thousand  dollars  cory and tommy can't cut a deal though  corey draws the line at twenty thousand  dollars while tommy doesn't seem  interested in haggling and insists on  his asking price  still the restaurant owner doesn't seem  too disappointed and remains confident  that he'll have another opportunity to  get that 40k  or even more damn check out one of our  newest videos right here  plus even more looper videos about comic  books are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one

